🟢Production concerns

🔸Api fail during append
-> cache data remain visible and handle with retry
lazyPagingItems.retry() is used to retry a failed paging request without refreshing the entire list.

🔸Same page is returned twice [duplicate page data]
🔹Use:
@Insert(onConflict = OnConflictStrategy.REPLACE)
📌@PrimaryKey identifies a unique record; @Upsert inserts new records or updates existing ones.

🔸Refresh occurs while append is pending:
Paging3 handle this . because it gives REFRESH priority high so if refresh call it cancel append
🔹Use:
Room withTransaction	All-or-nothing database changes
Primary key + @Upsert	Prevent duplicate rows for the same ID

🔸Process dies after the API succeeds:
If the process dies after the API succeeds, the main risk is that the server has completed the operation, but the app hasn't saved that success locally.
🔹Use:
Idempotency key[Prevent duplicate server-side execution.]
📌resends the request with the same idempotency key if the backend guarantees safe deduplication.
🔹Flow:
Room: Persist the operation and its status across process death.
WorkManager: Retry eligible work after the app process dies.
Idempotency key: Prevent duplicate server-side execution.

🔸API returns malformed or repeated cursors
I compare the requested cursor with the returned cursor. If it repeats, I stop pagination to prevent an infinite API request loop.
🔹Flow:
1-Request a page.
2-Check the next cursor.
3-If the cursor repeats, stop pagination by
return MediatorResult.Success(
        endOfPaginationReached = true
    )
and report log to further in backend investigation


🔸What happens for different failures?
Error	                      What to do
No internet / timeout	      Show error; allow retry
HTTP 500	                  Retry later with backoff
HTTP 401	                  Refresh authentication if appropriate
HTTP 400	                  Usually don't retry the same request unchanged
Invalid or repeated cursor	  Stop the pagination loop and report the issue

🔸What happens if repeated failure
limit retry count and make it fail..


🔸Concurrency in Pagging 3
Multiple paging operations are happening  at same time
🔹Handle:
1-Room Transaction — all operations succeed together
📌Suppose REFRESH fetches new users. You need to delete old users and insert new ones.
2-Atomic Update — One change happens safely
📌Suppose two operations update the same fund balance at nearly the same time.
3-Unique Key & @Upsert — prevent duplicate rows
📌Suppose the API returns page 2 twice. Both responses contain user ID 101.

🔸Imp:
Concept	                   Problem it solves
Transaction	               Partial database updates
Atomic update	           Lost updates from concurrent read-modify-write operations
Unique key + @Upsert	   Duplicate rows for the same entity